    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d720">

                <pb facs="1149" n="1053" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1053"/>

                <head>No. 718.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sail
                        to Mr. Davis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-05"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 5, 1873</date>.
                        (Received-November 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 294.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have time only to transmit herewith by
                    this steamer the inclosed official bulletin, just published, announcing the
                    capture of the steamer Virginius, on the 31st October, ultimo, near the coast of
                    Jamaica, and that a competent tribunal is now trying the prisoners, one hundred
                    and sixty-five in number, whom it styles pirates.</p>
                <p>I have just transmitted the Department the substance of the foregoing in a
                    telegram, it appearing to me that the vessel must have been captured, if not in
                    British at least in neutral waters, and that important international questions
                    may arise therefrom.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>HENRY C. HALL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Vice-Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d720-a1.xml" xpointer="d720-a1"/>
            </div>
